          %p
            The dual notion is a
            %strong factorization structure for cosinks
            (“sources”).
          %h3#on_size_and_foundations On size and foundations
          %p
            Observe that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+category"} large
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}
            contains
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+classes"} proper classes
            as elements. Therefore, in some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations"} foundations
            such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZF"} ZF
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NBG"} NBG
            one may treat it as a “hyperclass” defined by a first-order formula, in the same way that one treats classes in ZF. If we use a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+universe"} Grothendieck universe
            to define smallness, of course, there is no problem.
          %h2#constructions Constructions
          %p Many well-known factorization systems, and ways to construct factorization systems, extend to factorization structures for sinks and/or cosinks.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "/nlab/show/M-complete+category#ConstructingOFS"} This theorem
                implies that if a category is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-complete+category"} M-complete
                for a class
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                of morphisms which consists of monomorphisms and is closed under composition and pullback, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                is the right class in a factorization structure for sinks.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon A\to B
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck fibration
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                is an opfibration, we can lift factorization structures for cosinks. For the “mismatched” types of lifting, we require more:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                must be a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+concrete+category"} topological functor
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                In
                = succeed "," do
