                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi Mor
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^{|Mor(C)|}
              different morphisms
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y\to A
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cantor%27s+theorem"} Cantor's theorem
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor(C)
          %p
            This proof is of course quite reminiscent of Freyd’s theorem that any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+small+category"} complete small category
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
            %em small
            sinks, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is the class of all morphisms and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            the class of families of injections into coproducts. (Any complete small category is also cocomplete, by the
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
          %p
            Since Freyd’s theorem can fail in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            to also be essential in proving the above property of factorization structures.
